# Platform — Self-signup (UC-127)
# The two Platform calls of a signup, both tenant-less under /internal/*, InternalApiGuard only.
# The BFF is the only caller: it validates (here), reserves the registration (Billing), then
# provisions (here). Turnstile is verified once, in `validate`, never again in `tenant`.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl     = {{backendUrl}}
@internalKey = {{$dotenv INTERNAL_API_KEY}}

### Stateless validation: the slug policy and availability, then Turnstile. Persists nothing.
### 204 on success; 422 SIGNUP_SLUG_INVALID / SIGNUP_SLUG_RESERVED, 409 SIGNUP_SLUG_TAKEN,
### 400 SIGNUP_TURNSTILE_FAILED. The local Turnstile secret is Cloudflare's always-pass test key.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/signup/validate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slug": "lavacar-top-nova",
  "turnstileToken": "XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.9"
}

###

### Provision the tenant for a registration reserved first (registrationId from
### ../billing/registrations.http). The email becomes the first manager. 201; 409 SIGNUP_SLUG_TAKEN
### when the slug was taken between the check and the commit.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/signup/tenant
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lavacar Top Nova",
  "slug": "lavacar-top-nova",
  "adminEmail": "dona@example.com",
  "countryCode": "BR",
  "registrationId": "00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000"
}
